# Security Guidelines

## Core Security Rules

- All cryptographic operations must use Web Crypto API
- No server-side operations (static adapter requirement)
- Sensitive data must be encrypted before storage
- Use dual encryption for critical data (sub user id + recovery password)
- Implement proper key derivation for passwords
- Store encrypted keys using secure storage (NativeBiometric when available for mobile platform)
- Never expose private keys or encryption keys in plaintext
- Check Capacitor plugins availability on the platform before using them
- Always update test files according to changes in the code if needed

## Cryptographic Operations

### Web Crypto API Usage

```typescript
// Generate encryption key
const key = await crypto.subtle.generateKey(
  { name: 'AES-GCM', length: 256 },
  true,
  ['encrypt', 'decrypt']
);

// Encrypt data
const encrypted = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(
  { name: 'AES-GCM', iv: iv },
  key,
  new TextEncoder().encode(plaintext)
);

// Decrypt data
const decrypted = await crypto.subtle.decrypt(
  { name: 'AES-GCM', iv: iv },
  key,
  encrypted
);
```

### Key Management

```typescript
// Generate secure random keys
const generateSecureKey = (): Uint8Array => {
  return crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(32));
};

// Derive keys from passwords
const deriveKey = async (password: string, salt: Uint8Array): Promise<CryptoKey> => {
  const keyMaterial = await crypto.subtle.importKey(
    'raw',
    new TextEncoder().encode(password),
    { name: 'PBKDF2' },
    false,
    ['deriveBits', 'deriveKey']
  );

  return crypto.subtle.deriveKey(
    { name: 'PBKDF2', salt, iterations: 100000, hash: 'SHA-256' },
    keyMaterial,
    { name: 'AES-GCM', length: 256 },
    false,
    ['encrypt', 'decrypt']
  );
};
```

## Data Encryption

### Dual Encryption Pattern

```typescript
// First layer: User-specific encryption
const encryptUserData = async (data: string, userKey: CryptoKey): Promise<string> => {
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const encrypted = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(
    { name: 'AES-GCM', iv },
    userKey,
    new TextEncoder().encode(data)
  );
  return btoa(String.fromCharCode(...iv, ...new Uint8Array(encrypted)));
};

// Second layer: Recovery password encryption
const encryptWithRecovery = async (encryptedData: string, recoveryKey: CryptoKey): Promise<string> => {
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const encrypted = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(
    { name: 'AES-GCM', iv },
    recoveryKey,
    new TextEncoder().encode(encryptedData)
  );
  return btoa(String.fromCharCode(...iv, ...new Uint8Array(encrypted)));
};
```

### Secure Storage

```typescript
// Check platform capabilities
const isNativeBiometricAvailable = async (): Promise<boolean> => {
  try {
    const { NativeBiometric } = await import('capacitor-native-biometric');
    return await NativeBiometric.isAvailable();
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
};

// Store encrypted data securely
const storeSecurely = async (key: string, value: string): Promise<void> => {
  if (await isNativeBiometricAvailable()) {
    // Use biometric-secured storage
    const { NativeBiometric } = await import('capacitor-native-biometric');
    await NativeBiometric.setCredentials({
      username: key,
      password: value,
      server: 'bittasker'
    });
  } else {
    // Fallback to encrypted localStorage
    const encrypted = await encryptWithAppKey(value);
    localStorage.setItem(key, encrypted);
  }
};
```

## Input Validation

### Schema Validation

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

// Define strict schemas
const userSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string().uuid(),
  email: z.string().email(),
  name: z.string().min(1).max(100),
  age: z.number().int().min(0).max(150)
});

// Validate and sanitize input
const validateUser = (input: unknown): User => {
  return userSchema.parse(input);
};
```

### XSS Prevention

```typescript
// Sanitize HTML content
const sanitizeHtml = (html: string): string => {
  const div = document.createElement('div');
  div.textContent = html;
  return div.innerHTML;
};

// Escape user input
const escapeHtml = (text: string): string => {
  return text
    .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
    .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
    .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
    .replace(/"/g, '&quot;')
    .replace(/'/g, '&#39;');
};
```

## Authentication Security

### Key Generation

```typescript
// Generate secure random keys for authentication
const generateAuthKey = (): string => {
  const array = new Uint8Array(32);
  crypto.getRandomValues(array);
  return Array.from(array, byte => byte.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('');
};
```

### Session Management

```typescript
// Secure session token generation
const generateSessionToken = async (): Promise<string> => {
  const randomBytes = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(32));
  const hash = await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', randomBytes);
  return Array.from(new Uint8Array(hash), byte => byte.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('');
};
```

## Error Handling Security

### Secure Error Messages

```typescript
// Don't expose sensitive information in errors
const handleError = (error: unknown): string => {
  console.error('Internal error:', error);
  return 'An error occurred. Please try again.';
};

// Log errors securely
const logError = (error: Error, context: string): void => {
  console.error(`[${context}] ${error.message}`, {
    stack: error.stack,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  });
};
```

## Platform-Specific Security

### Capacitor Plugin Security

```typescript
// Check plugin availability before use
const useSecureStorage = async (): Promise<boolean> => {
  try {
    const { NativeBiometric } = await import('capacitor-native-biometric');
    return await NativeBiometric.isAvailable();
  } catch (error) {
    console.warn('Native biometric not available:', error);
    return false;
  }
};
```

## Testing Security

### Security Test Requirements

```typescript
// Test encryption/decryption
describe('Encryption', () => {
  it('should encrypt and decrypt data correctly', async () => {
    const key = await generateEncryptionKey();
    const data = 'sensitive information';
    
    const encrypted = await encrypt(data, key);
    const decrypted = await decrypt(encrypted, key);
    
    expect(decrypted).toBe(data);
    expect(encrypted).not.toBe(data);
  });
});

// Test key derivation
describe('Key Derivation', () => {
  it('should derive consistent keys from same password', async () => {
    const password = 'test-password';
    const salt = new Uint8Array(16);
    
    const key1 = await deriveKey(password, salt);
    const key2 = await deriveKey(password, salt);
    
    expect(key1).toEqual(key2);
  });
});
```

## Security Checklist

Before deploying any security-sensitive code:

- [ ] All sensitive data is encrypted
- [ ] Keys are properly derived and stored securely
- [ ] Input validation is implemented
- [ ] Error messages don't expose sensitive information
- [ ] Platform capabilities are checked before use
- [ ] Tests cover security scenarios
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets or keys
- [ ] Proper key rotation mechanisms
- [ ] Secure communication protocols
- [ ] Access controls are implemented
